  "details": "<p>Assyrian and Suhean texts also mention a city called\u00a0Ra\u1e63appa, which may have been the capital/principal administrative center of the land/province of the same name.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A land (and later an Assyrian province) mentioned in first-millennium B.C. Akkadian texts from Assyria and Suhu. Scholars generally believe that this land/province is located east of the Habur River, south of Jebel Singar, and northeast of the land Bit-Halup\u00ea.",
